  "domain": "artificial-intelligence",
  "definition": "Proof theory is the branch of mathematical logic that studies formal proofs as syntactic objects \u2014 their structure, rules of inference, and the transformations between them \u2014 independent of the semantic models that make statements true. It underpins automated theorem proving, type theory, and formal verification, providing the rules by which a machine can check or search for a valid derivation of a conclusion from axioms. Results such as cut-elimination and normalisation are central to its use in computer science.",
